  "step_3": "The information relevant to the decision reason—probabilities of favorable outcomes and the treatment of outcome differences as negligible—matches what the individual considered. The individual acknowledged the higher probability of winning in Lottery A (90%) and explicitly stated that the amount (sum) was less important, aligning with the reason’s assumption that outcome differences are negligible. Furthermore, the individual’s justification—prioritizing the higher chance of winning over the larger sum—directly corresponds to the rule of the decision reason, which prefers the lottery with the higher probability of a favorable outcome when outcome differences are not decisive. Therefore, both the information considered and the justification align closely with the decision reason.",
